      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but it doesnt feel random. the pulsing rhythm is too consistent for just a heater or something. if i look at the specific patterns in those atmospheric shifts from the 17th, is there any theoretical way that specialized low-frequency waves could be modulated to carry information? like, could high-pressure cells act as a sort of carrier for something? i feel like if there was a reason for the signal, it would be found in the physics of the air itself.",
