      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the idea of cloaking a signal within a massive natural phenomenon is logically appealing for evasion, there is no established, widely documented precedent for reliably encoding and decoding complex data through natural atmospheric pressure modulations like high-pressure cells. Infrasound *can* carry energy and is sometimes studied for scientific purposes, but sophisticated data transfer usually relies on electromagnetic spectrum methods for practicality. If you have ongoing concerns about being monitored, seeking advice from local authorities or a technical expert would be a more grounded first step than pursuing highly speculative atmospheric theories.",
